#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Every function's description and grants, in one place. Regenerates
# functions/<name>/<name>.json; never edit those by hand (bin/fnjson.py, as Sprints').
#   table   read        table:rw  + write rows        table:rwd  + delete rows
#   function:<name>     run it        /folder:verbs   a folder
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
f() { uv run --no-project python bin/fnjson.py "$@"; }
READ="product feature feedback ask deal company project task roadmap_settings roadmap_item roadmap_spec deals_settings"
f roadmap_rank "The team's features ranked by who asked: people (distinct handles across feedback and asks), companies, blockers, open and won deal value per currency, last asked, quotes, stage and horizon. No score. sort: people (default), companies, blockers, open, won, last_asked, quotes, stage, horizon; since_days; company (id or name); horizon: all, not_planned, now, next, later, shipped. Its text is a ready answer." $READ
f roadmap_feature "One feature (by id or name): its numbers, who asked grouped by company (blockers first, one quote each, where said, the company's deal), its quotes 20 at a time (all, blockers, not_in_spec), the team's plan, the spec and its project's progress." $READ
f roadmap_set "Put a feature on the roadmap or move it (horizon now, next, later, none), decline it, give it an owner (owner_user_id or owner_label), or set how the outside page shows it (public, public_title, public_blurb). Moves feature.stage forward only: next or later -> planned, now -> building, decline -> declined; never live, never back." feature:rw roadmap_item:rw roadmap_public:rwd roadmap_settings deals_settings
f roadmap_ship "Mark a roadmap item shipped (shipped_on, default today; undo puts it back in Now). Leaves feature.stage to Release notes, which sets it live and tells the people who asked. Says how many people there are to tell." feature ask roadmap_item:rw roadmap_public:rwd roadmap_settings deals_settings
f roadmap_project "Make a Tasks project for a feature on the roadmap (source roadmap, named after the feature, led by its owner) and link it; or link an existing project (project_id). Pressing twice makes one project." feature project:rw roadmap_item:rw
f roadmap_publish "Rewrite the outside roadmap page's table (roadmap_public) from the items marked public: title, blurb, now/next/later, and what shipped in the last 90 days. Empty while the page is off." feature roadmap_item roadmap_public:rwd roadmap_settings deals_settings
f roadmap_tick "The roadmap lead's daily run: writes their decide items in Today (a Now item whose tasks stopped moving, an item whose tasks are all done, a suggested feature with 5 or more quotes) and closes the rest. Writes nothing when run by anyone but the lead." $READ needs_you:rw
f roadmap_spec_draft "Draft a feature's spec around the roadmap-spec-writer agent. brief: picks up to ~60 KB of its quotes (blockers first, two per company, then newest), keyed q1..; save: drops any key the brief didn't give, marks lines with no quote, keeps edited lines, writes /pages/roadmap/<feature>.md and roadmap_spec." $READ roadmap_spec:rw /pages:read,write
f roadmap_spec_save_edit "Save a feature's spec as a person edited it (every line: section, key, text, quotes): changed lines are kept on a redraft, a line with its quotes taken off shows No quote; rewrites the Page." feature feedback roadmap_spec:rw /pages:read,write
f roadmap_setup_save "Roadmap's set-up: the lead, the currency money is shown in first, stale days, the product's name and the outside page on or off. Makes the team's product when there is none, rewrites the outside page's table and writes Roadmap's memory block. Safe to run again." roadmap_settings:rw product:rw feature roadmap_item roadmap_public:rwd deals_settings function:roadmap_memory
f roadmap_memory "Tells this Lemma's agents that Roadmap is installed: Roadmap's block in /memory/AGENTS.md and its guide at /memory/plugins/roadmap.md, leaving the team's notes alone. Set-up runs it; safe to run again. remove takes both out." /memory:read,write
f roadmap_sample_data "load: a made-up product's roadmap (features, quotes from made-up companies, asks, deals, three Tasks projects and the team's plan) to look around. clear: removes only what the sample made, and the specs, Pages and projects made for it since." product:rwd company:rwd company_domain:rwd deal:rwd feature:rwd feedback:rwd ask:rwd project:rwd task:rwd roadmap_item:rwd roadmap_spec:rwd roadmap_public:rwd roadmap_settings:rw roadmap_sample_row:rwd needs_you:rw deals_settings /pages:read,write,delete
